    "text": "<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>of two distinct real numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp; and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and&#160;</mtext><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are three geometric means between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></math>&nbsp;equals</p>"
